==Strategy==
This stage is immensely challenging due to the infinitely respawning support threats that appear on timers to accompany the Crazed Tank Cat on base hit, to the point even their fairly high money drop will not be able to fund a constant stream of units. Nevertheless, other attackers should be brought for the peons, as they will provide a bit of DPS and usually stay outside of Crazed Tank's range until their targets are gone. Starting with a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] are usually mandatory, with a [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] optionally used to facilitate rapid replacement of at least 5 small meatshields. The Crazed Tank's stage is by far one of the most important in the game, rewarding an exceptional meatshield unit. Trios of enemies will spawn on timers, with the Crazed Tank on base hit. Try to stall hitting the base until defeating the first set of Owlbrows, as you will need as much cash as you can to battle Crazed Tank.

Crazed Tank's range is no laughing matter. It's surprisingly high, at 390, and hits for more than 30k with a very fast attack cycle of around 2.23. Units that cannot outrange it will be destroyed in seconds, and even those that do will struggle over time, since its very short backswing allows it to advance a little more with each attack, despite moving at 2 speed, as its singular Knockback prevents it from flinching through raw damage until it has been destroyed. The use of Knockback effects will be required to hold it back, as are anything that forces it to get displaced (Sniper the Cat, default Cat Cannon, etc). [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] will most likely be your main fighting force, both having enough range to safely hit Crazed Tank and Owlbrow. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] works even better, though players may or may not have her this early into the game.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]/[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Heavy]] - With their slow and knockback abilities respectively, Cyberpunk and Sniper can impede the Crazed Tank from extreme range. They don't come without downsides, however - Cyberpunk is expensive, has poor uptime (~25%) without talents, while Sniper's single attack can be blocked by peons. Both have long recharge times, so something else must provide cover during their downtime.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] - A powerful backliner standing at 450 range with very high damage (85,000 at level 30, only Duche and Crazed Tank can survive more than a single hit) Bahamut will be a consistent source of DPS throughout the entire stage for players who lack other options, even if his long attack cycle is factored in. Bahamut stacking with Speed Ups can be a viable option, though this is still incredibly tedious.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]] - Delivering powerful single attacks from an impressive 620 range with a 10% chance to crit, Tesalan can speed up the fight substantially as it helps whittling down Crazed Tank, provided if the other enemies are cleared.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]], [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] and other [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] Ubers that are able to safely outrange the boss and potentially hit the base behind him with the use of a Sniper the Cat and sufficient protection. Should you have any of them, they can make this stage much easier.
*Any [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless]] Ubers, especially the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives, can help massively with their abilities. However, using low-ranged rushers ([[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], [[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Landshaker Kozuchimaru]] etc.) are not recommended as they are likely to be hit before they can do anything.

